\begin{proposition}\label{prop:image}
% Let $(X,\sigma,\tau)=\mathcal{S}(G\times \Z_n,\mathbf{c},f)$. 
 An equivalence relation $\asymp$ is a congruence of the solution $(X,\sigma,\tau)=\mathcal{S}(G\times \Z_n,\mathbf{c})$ if and only if there exist a~subgroup~$H$ of~$(G+,0)$,  $m\in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ and $r\in G$ such that:
