 $n=2r$, $c_0=0$, $c_i=\sum_{k=1}^i e_k$
 and $c_{i+r}=\sum_{k=i+1}^r e_k$,  for $i\in\{1,\ldots,r\}$. Then the solution $(X,\sigma,\tau)=\mathcal{S}(G\times \Z_n,{\bf c})$ is uniconnected, $(G,+,0)\cong\dis{X}$ and ${\mathcal{G}}(X)\cong G\rtimes_\alpha\Z_n$, where $\alpha(1)(e_i)=e_{i+1}$, for $i<r$, and $\alpha(1)(e_r)=-e_1$.
 
