and therefore the permutation group $\mathcal{G}(X)$  is transitive on~$G\times \Z_n$.

Let $(a,i),(b,j)\in G\times \Z_n$. By the construction of permutations $L_{(a,i)}$ and $\sigma_{(b,j)}$, the intersection $\dis{G\times \Z_n}\cap\langle{\sigma_{(b,j)}}\rangle$ is trivial. Hence,  Proposition \ref{prop:normal} finishes the proof.
