codex
The paper supports the family: Theorem 4.1 gives the native construction from a spanning sequence, Proposition 4.4 identifies the abelian easy case, and Theorem 4.7 makes isomorphism exactly a group-isomorphism-on-sequences problem. Track A is therefore false, but Track B is viable: generic modular elimination is the disclosed mechanical route, while the planted double rank-one structure gives a sub-300-operation route.

The draft needs two material fixes before testing: its “random guess” prior ignores the first mapping equation that any solver gets essentially for free, and its rendered JSON example has the wrong dimension outside the demo preset. I’m correcting both and strengthening the cheap attacks to start from that same free information.
