codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on Theorems 4.1 and 4.7 and Proposition 4.4 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.02944).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2207_02944.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/gen_2207_02944.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2207.02944/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Highlights:

- 12/12 planted witnesses verified.
- 76,832 involutivity pairs and 20,000 Yang–Baxter triples checked.
- Informed guess probability is approximately \(5.66\times10^{-73}\); 0/200,000 samples succeeded.
- Five attacks failed across 8/8 seeds each.
- Reference elimination: 4,984 field operations; compact route: at most 195.
- Canonical-key invariance: 160/160 transformations.
- Worst-case shipping answer: 205 characters, 32 atoms.

One external blocker remains: every bare, hinted, and placebo oracle call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, no hardness verdict exists and `easy` remains a candidate shipping preset rather than a release-approved one. Refreshing the OpenRouter quota and rerunning `python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2207_02944.py` is required to complete STEP 4.
